{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790271325,"nonce":"X28QoWXJNCqArhtSGF4EbuiZkd0=","message":"Correction on attribution: on main (dea6d08b) a dynamic unpack of a set or range that is too long prints 'too many values to unpack (expected 2)', which matches CPython 3.14. Commit 5cea29f4 (not yet on main) adds ', got N' to the kind-level zb_list_expect_len message, so after it set, range and str sources print '(expected 2, got 3)', while list, tuple and dict become right. Before landing, the ', got N' suffix should be limited to list, tuple and dict sources. Reproducer: for v in [{1, 2, 3}, range(3), 'abc']: a, b = v (inside try/except ValueError, printing e).","files":null}]}